9566       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.NEWS has 40 observations and 3 variables.

9587       ;
9588       proc format;
9589       value subscrib 1 = 'accept' 0 = 'reject';
NOTE: Format SUBSCRIB has been output.
9590       run;


9591       proc probit data=news;
9592       class sex;
9593       model subs(event="accept")=sex age / d=logistic itprint;
9594       format subs subscrib.;
9595       store out=LogitModel;
9596       run;

NOTE: PROC PROBIT is modeling the probabilities of levels of subs having LOWER Ordered Values in the response profile table.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: The PROBIT procedure generated the model item store WORK.LOGITMODEL.
